KaTeX (bundled webview assets — media/katex/)
---------------------------------------------
The math-preview webview renders LaTeX with KaTeX. Its distribution files
(`katex.min.js`, `katex.min.css`, and the `KaTeX_*` woff2 web fonts) are
vendored verbatim under `media/katex/` and shipped inside the `.vsix`; they are
loaded only inside the preview webview, never into the extension host.

  https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX
  License: MIT
  Pinned: katex 0.16.x (see the `katex` devDependency in package.json)

Vendored copy provenance: copied from `node_modules/katex/dist/` after
`npm install`. Only the woff2 fonts are shipped (the CSS lists woff2 first and
the webview's Chromium picks it; the woff/ttf faces are omitted to keep the
package lean). To refresh, re-copy `katex.min.js`, `katex.min.css`, and
`fonts/*.woff2` from the pinned dist and re-verify the MIT license still holds.

Mermaid (bundled webview asset — media/mermaid/)
------------------------------------------------
The diagram-preview webview renders Mermaid (```` ```{mermaid} ````) diagrams
with the Mermaid library. A single, self-contained distribution file
(`mermaid.min.js`) is vendored verbatim under `media/mermaid/` and shipped inside
the `.vsix`; it is loaded only inside the preview webview, never into the
extension host.

  https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2014 - 2022 Knut Sveidqvist)
  Pinned: mermaid 11.16.0
  File: dist/mermaid.min.js (sha256
        74d7c46dabca328c2294733910a8aa1ed0c37451776e8d5295da38a2b758fb9b)

Vendored copy provenance: extracted from the npm registry tarball
https://registry.npmjs.org/mermaid/-/mermaid-11.16.0.tgz (`package/dist/
mermaid.min.js`). Unlike KaTeX, Mermaid is NOT added as a devDependency: the
distribution file is a single self-contained UMD bundle (it exposes
`globalThis.mermaid`, performs no runtime `import()`, and needs no
`'unsafe-eval'`), so only this one file ships and pulling Mermaid's large
transitive dev-dependency tree into `node_modules` solely to copy it is
unnecessary. To refresh, re-download the pinned (or newer) tarball, verify the
MIT license still holds, copy `dist/mermaid.min.js`, and update the version +
sha256 above.

Graphviz (bundled webview asset — media/graphviz/)
---------------------------------------------------
The diagram-preview webview renders Graphviz (```` ```{dot} ````) diagrams with
`@viz-js/viz`, a WASM compile of the real upstream Graphviz C library. A
single, self-contained distribution file (`viz-global.js`) is vendored verbatim
under `media/graphviz/` and shipped inside the `.vsix`; it is loaded only
inside the preview webview, never into the extension host.

  https://github.com/mdaines/viz-js  (the `@viz-js/viz` npm package)
  Wrapper license: MIT (Copyright (c) Michael Daines)
  Pinned: @viz-js/viz 3.28.0
  File: dist/viz-global.js (sha256
        050980a2a3721a493ec2fae035a964728f14765212b821d2b994dff03a03c0e2)

**This is the first vendored asset in this project whose bundled contents are
NOT entirely MIT.** `@viz-js/viz`'s own file header states verbatim: "This
distribution contains other software in object code form: Graphviz
https://www.graphviz.org / Expat https://libexpat.github.io" — confirmed by
its shipped `lib/provenance.json` SLSA build-attestation, which records a real
compile of upstream Graphviz 15.0.0 (`gitlab.com/graphviz/graphviz`) and
libexpat 2.8.1 via Emscripten:

  - Graphviz core (compiled into the WASM module): **Eclipse Public License
    2.0 (EPL-2.0)** — https://www.graphviz.org (license terms:
    https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/). EPL-2.0 is a weak (file-scoped)
    copyleft license: it permits redistributing the covered code in
    object/binary form under different license terms provided the license is
    disclosed and corresponding source is made available — both satisfied
    here, by this notice and by Graphviz's own public upstream repository. It
    does not require this extension's own source (MIT) to relicense.
  - Expat/libexpat (XML parsing, compiled into the WASM module): **MIT** —
    https://libexpat.github.io

Vendored copy provenance: extracted from the npm registry tarball
https://registry.npmjs.org/@viz-js/viz/-/viz-3.28.0.tgz (`package/dist/
viz-global.js`). Like Mermaid, `@viz-js/viz` is NOT added as a devDependency:
the distribution file is a single self-contained UMD bundle (exposes
`globalThis.Viz`, confirmed to call zero `eval()`/`new Function()` — only
`WebAssembly.instantiate`, which is why the diagram-preview webview's CSP adds
`'wasm-unsafe-eval'` and nothing broader), so only this one file ships. To
refresh, re-download the pinned (or newer) tarball, re-verify the Graphviz/
Expat license chain still holds (re-check `lib/provenance.json` and the
file's own header comment), copy `dist/viz-global.js`, and update the version
+ sha256 above.

On upgrade of any referenced grammar or tool, re-verify the license still holds
at the pinned version and update this file (architecture plan §9, §14).
